--------------------Based on the requirements given in the comments, the following assert statements could be included:

```cs
// @@@ If the return value is false, last position of x in old list is >= -1
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == false || Old_arrListLastIndexOfX >= -1);
```

This line of code will assert that if the new result of the `Contains()` method is false (the value `x` is not found in the list), then the last position of `x` in the original list (`Old_arrListLastIndexOfX`) must be greater than or equal to -1. This indicates that `x` has either been removed from the list (if `Old_arrListLastIndexOfX` is -1), is still in the list (if `Old_arrListLastIndexOfX` is 0 or more), or was not found in the list at all (if `Old_arrListLastIndexOfX` is less than -1, which should never happen as IndexOf and LastIndexOf should never return negative values).
